{
  "title": "Wat is het leukst?",
  "goal": "Review comparisons and use regular and common irregular superlatives to compare familiar cities, food and activities.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "content": "Wat is het leukst?",
      "id": "4be5e46f-3de5-4d57-b3e6-ab81fdd198d9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It is Wednesday 13 January 2027. Sofia and Noor compare familiar places, food and activities. You will review comparatives and learn superlatives.",
      "id": "cc09deae-2c50-4d57-96c2-7bd085daada7"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Verbs are blue, subjects green, and de- and het-forms pink and brown. The new superlative forms are bold.",
      "id": "4eedfb6f-9b3c-4d21-9e6f-b58206778519"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Story: a friendly comparison",
      "id": "677f5f13-fe54-4652-a92f-c2e67528df99"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Noor, welke stad is groter: Utrecht of Valencia?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Utrecht is kleiner dan Valencia, maar Valencia is warmer."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "En welke stad is het grootst?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Valencia is het grootst."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Wat vindt Henk lekkerder: de paella of de boerenkoolstamppot?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Henk vindt de boerenkoolstamppot lekkerder dan de paella."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "En de pierogi?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Die zijn ook lekker. Kasia vindt ze heerlijk."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, ik vind alles lekker."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "En welke activiteit vind je het leukst?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ik zwem het liefst. Schaatsen vind ik best eng."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Dan vind je zwemmen misschien het leukst!"
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "2452b6a0-28b9-414a-8681-7c6f3076aaec"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "id": "3cd51107-f988-4f32-bec1-3dd6d96c8414"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Review: comparatives",
      "id": "ca458764-566b-41e2-a87a-e8788cadbe5c"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Comparative + dan",
      "id": "cd623c5a-d723-4ddc-9650-ba190f840059"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You already know adjective + -er + dan, and even/net zo/niet zo … als. This lesson adds the superlative; it does not repeat the full comparative lesson.",
      "id": "0842d14b-1732-4a56-915c-7cf52bd12965"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Utrecht is smaller than Valencia.",
        "note": "Recycles 18-b: comparative + dan."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Utrecht",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "kleiner",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        " dan Valencia."
      ],
      "id": "abf8acf3-b449-4353-94ea-5894720f9a71"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "The street is just as narrow as that street.",
        "note": "Recycles net zo … als from 18-b."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "De",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "pink"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "straat",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "net zo smal als",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "die",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "pink"
          }
        },
        " straat."
      ],
      "id": "f92cbbc2-8964-4047-bfb8-f2fcd847ee6b"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "helder",
              "meaning": "clear, bright",
              "example": "De lucht is helder.",
              "id": "9155a3cc-6415-463a-ac69-88c92a3ae6a4"
            },
            {
              "term": "donker",
              "meaning": "dark",
              "example": "De lucht is donker.",
              "id": "19380ea1-238d-4f7f-bff9-fc1de2696f29",
              "note": "Previously used in colour compounds such as donkerblauw (18-a); this lesson uses it as a standalone adjective."
            },
            {
              "term": "smal",
              "meaning": "narrow",
              "example": "Deze straat is smal.",
              "id": "ce9e9159-4a11-4eac-918d-bddaeef44adb"
            },
            {
              "term": "breed",
              "meaning": "wide",
              "example": "Die straat is breed.",
              "id": "c9c8ce6f-cf7b-4b7e-9f4a-6e22ea966d5c"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "8c0e9eed-3445-43cd-964c-68db493f7197"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "content": "Comparative: adjective + -er + dan. Equality: even/net zo/niet zo + base adjective + als.",
      "id": "23411e1f-51d4-406d-b78c-9fbb3560e781"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Superlatives",
      "id": "971b6d16-85ad-4ec9-acb3-ef89d8de09f2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Most: het + -st",
      "id": "881b8d74-030d-4e5c-853c-47037ae2bd1b"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Use the superlative to name the top degree in a group. With zijn or as an adverb, use het + the superlative form: Utrecht is het rustigst. In writing, the adverb form usually ends in -st.",
      "id": "3e6cd936-8817-4372-b6d8-940516e9d8e2"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Utrecht is the quietest in the morning.",
        "note": "Predicative adjective used as a superlative; het + rustigst."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Utrecht",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "het",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "brown"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "rustigst",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        " in de ochtend."
      ],
      "id": "ad2b34db-f02d-426c-b1f9-b1b849702a53"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Which activity do you like most?",
        "note": "het leukst is a superlative adverbial phrase; compare the options."
      },
      "content": [
        "Welke activiteit ",
        {
          "text": "vind",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "je",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "het",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "brown"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "leukst",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        "?"
      ],
      "id": "d7ff961a-d5ce-4410-aaf8-e2947202a0b7"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "important",
        "icon": "star"
      },
      "content": "The adverbial or predicative form commonly uses het + -st: het rustigst, het leukst.",
      "id": "2c116edb-002c-4a76-b623-97dc536403aa"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Before a noun: -ste",
      "id": "fe8cfb90-9ab6-4c19-9361-ccc26cabc349"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Before a noun, use the article that belongs to that noun, then an adjective ending in -ste. The adjective also takes -e, as other adjectives do before nouns.",
      "id": "3eec8194-d4c1-463c-a022-00b17477042e"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "The quietest street is here.",
        "note": "De straat is a de-word: de rustigste straat."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "De",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "pink"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "rustigste",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green",
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "straat",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " hier."
      ],
      "id": "55e37f4c-80d0-4383-a039-74dbe3512838"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "The quietest café is small.",
        "note": "Het café is a het-word: het rustigste café."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Het",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "brown"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "rustigste",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green",
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "café",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " klein."
      ],
      "id": "d39c25d6-2919-4d56-a257-6467f6271168"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "comfortabel",
              "meaning": "comfortable",
              "example": "Deze stoel is comfortabel.",
              "id": "8188049c-13fd-4727-80d2-dc03df91b7b5"
            },
            {
              "term": "aantrekkelijk",
              "meaning": "attractive",
              "example": "De stad is aantrekkelijk.",
              "id": "f5cd9693-0688-4fe7-8fd5-77157387bfd5"
            },
            {
              "term": "rommelig",
              "meaning": "messy",
              "example": "De kamer is rommelig.",
              "id": "1d722dfb-80d1-40d7-b13a-6017a61a53c2"
            },
            {
              "term": "netjes",
              "meaning": "tidy",
              "example": "De tafel is netjes.",
              "id": "84a17ecb-f0b4-427c-901f-9b49e787fc8d"
            },
            {
              "term": "modern",
              "meaning": "modern",
              "example": "Het gebouw is modern.",
              "id": "759d51bb-3ec9-41ca-a247-7e7b6cb70369"
            },
            {
              "term": "ouderwets",
              "meaning": "old-fashioned",
              "example": "Deze stoel is ouderwets.",
              "id": "f2018e23-87f0-43f3-91a4-2a09e232e95b"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "7efc1b0c-0a4e-48b5-835e-859729e727cd"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "content": "Before a noun: de/het + adjective + -ste + noun. The article follows the noun’s gender.",
      "id": "67248622-8f51-4d7e-bc17-fb8c68cf333c"
    },
    {
      "type": "columnList",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "Before a noun",
              "id": "2e821a3f-6e48-4e12-a4b0-dd68b9e01f02"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "de breedste straat",
              "id": "1d920a49-08fe-4772-a1c0-4eb8161f6420"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "het breedste plein",
              "id": "6a2509b4-bb26-4a19-abb8-70a13f7dbb1f"
            }
          ],
          "id": "914de089-7e05-485d-848d-c2fdac6c1b76"
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "As a predicate/adverb",
              "id": "de95ef11-0a14-4643-826c-3e584aeeedff"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "De straat is het breedst.",
              "id": "f780fef5-bb03-4c61-89aa-84de43823c9b"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "Het plein is het breedst.",
              "id": "78840ea1-106a-4457-8f3a-0232487d093d"
            }
          ],
          "id": "bbf2d3b3-2ab4-49c6-bfa0-95aaba922c57"
        }
      ],
      "id": "4edc51c7-5e73-425c-8127-57d5f065e7b7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Spelling and irregular forms",
      "id": "855a9727-5cc9-4d55-9150-464e5f515c72"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Keep the adjective spelling",
      "id": "3e639734-540e-4d4c-a1d6-b431d3e2a5f5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Add -st for the common adverbial form; add -ste before a noun. Keep the base spelling pattern: a long vowel stays long, and a short vowel keeps its double consonant where needed. Some superlatives end in -tst: groot → grootst.",
      "id": "8724a5a4-fefd-4ca6-8daf-b2cf31af00e9"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "The biggest city is Valencia.",
        "note": "groot → grootst; before a de-word noun: grootste."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "De",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "pink"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "grootste",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green",
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "stad",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " Valencia."
      ],
      "id": "8e34f23b-a8e7-4fd0-a128-166eb09155e6"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "This rule is the simplest.",
        "note": "eenvoudig → eenvoudigst."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Deze regel",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "het",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "brown"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "eenvoudigst",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "id": "e2a9cbcb-6bd8-49cd-8d47-866bfa771915"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "populair",
              "meaning": "popular",
              "example": "Voetbal is populair.",
              "id": "7706383a-e6f6-4b97-b7b1-838475bd4697"
            },
            {
              "term": "eenvoudig",
              "meaning": "simple",
              "example": "De vraag is eenvoudig.",
              "id": "9d6f26bd-c200-4580-b6b7-83e894839fca"
            },
            {
              "term": "ingewikkeld",
              "meaning": "complicated",
              "example": "Deze regel is ingewikkeld.",
              "id": "ab100a8f-dc62-4821-a752-2ef4998a87ad"
            },
            {
              "term": "verrassend",
              "meaning": "surprising",
              "example": "De prijs is verrassend.",
              "id": "41e72a7c-0b15-45fa-967b-fc87f5259808"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "5d1dd1bc-f93e-443f-947c-7c88ca943d23"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "warning",
        "icon": "triangle-alert"
      },
      "content": [
        "Use the adjective spelling before the ending: ",
        {
          "text": "grotst",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true,
            "backgroundColor": "gray"
          }
        },
        " → ",
        {
          "text": "grootst",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "text": "de grootst stad",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true,
            "backgroundColor": "gray"
          }
        },
        " → ",
        {
          "text": "de grootste stad",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "id": "fca0282d-9668-4737-8b28-dd46f6d56cbf"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Common irregular forms",
      "id": "7a05855e-b440-4d40-a3d6-a86ded9dc963"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Two common comparisons have special forms. Learn the three forms together.",
      "id": "2b4c04af-32f4-44e4-8dbd-796ea696f191"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "de superlatief",
              "meaning": "superlative",
              "forms": "de superlatieven",
              "example": "De superlatief van goed is best.",
              "id": "b01a827e-3ecc-4241-9890-02dd32e16baa"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "6c342074-3475-4c47-a19a-be8361b009b7"
    },
    {
      "type": "columnList",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "goed",
              "id": "82a06245-9e73-4bbc-b0a3-3fb832342915"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "goed → beter → best",
              "id": "9c43c268-a707-4746-9155-1e4a44614acf"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "het best / de beste",
              "id": "3a42c150-cb7d-45d7-aa2e-31aae4aad9be"
            }
          ],
          "id": "db0ab249-09d0-4261-825c-1c0eda2da968"
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "veel",
              "id": "10549193-4574-4a40-b160-13619229c74a"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "veel → meer → meest",
              "id": "b0d8da6f-6254-4a00-a2a9-e11bab865b59"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "het meest / de meeste",
              "id": "58d5e98c-fccc-4416-817a-4725dbfd0f6c"
            }
          ],
          "id": "e3361b63-5b92-4c4f-8518-c62920433148"
        }
      ],
      "id": "4dd315e3-8760-4245-a242-36499c532ab9"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "The paella is good, but the stamppot is better.",
        "note": "Recycles the irregular comparative from 18-b."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "De",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "pink"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "paella",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " goed, maar ",
        {
          "text": "de",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "pink"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
          "text": "stamppot",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " ",
        {
